%C __DRIVER_DESCRIPTION__
__DRIVER_SPECIFIC_USE__
Driver options are one or more of the following, separated by commas
without whitespace:

prefix  - Only used in conjunction with "mount". Matches the prefix option used
          when launching io-sock to specify which instance of io-sock should
          mount this driver.

qnxdev  - Used when Plug And Play is disabled. Specifies the device instance
          that this driver will use. Use "devinfo -v" to determine the
          location to be passed with this option e.g. qnxdev=pci0:0:25:0
__DRIVER_SPECIFIC_OPTIONS__
